From 9f709ff3eea183f64ea89df1af544f0b29326c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:35:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 104/104] packetizer: helper: let a break cost one access unit,
 not the rest of the block

The shared body of the h264, hevc, mpeg video, mpeg4 video and vc1 packetizers
hands the remainder of a block back through block_BytestreamPop(), which does
not touch i_flags - upstream's "So p_block doesn't get re-added several times"
is saying that the block comes back - so a block that arrived on a
discontinuity resets the parser once for every access unit taken out of it,
and pf_reset() here also arms each of those packetizers' outbound flag, so
every extra reset stamps another picture that the decoder then acts on.

On real content it does not fire today. A reset only costs anything if an
access unit ends inside the flagged block, and no demuxer that stamps the flag
hands over more than one access unit at a time: ts, ps, mp4, matroska and avi
all deliver a picture per block, so the flagged block is consumed before
anything is popped. Four second mpeg-2 and h264 items in a transport stream,
looped three times with --input-repeat, measure one reset and one stamped
picture per seam before and after.

What does hand over blocks that straddle access units is the raw elementary
stream side - h26x reads 2048 bytes at a time and runs the packetizer itself -
and those demuxers stamp nothing, which is the only reason this is latent. So
it was measured by injecting the flag on every seventh block h26x reads, on a
four second 50 fps h264 stream of about ten frames to a block: eleven breaks
cost 19 parser resets and delivered 528 pictures, and with the flag cleared
17 resets and 626, three runs each, identical every time. Ninety-eight
pictures - two seconds of the four - for eleven breaks that should have cost
eleven frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h b/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
index 42b881bcd0..0c2a67e49c 100644
--- a/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
+++ b/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
@@ -130,6 +130,14 @@ static block_t *packetizer_PacketizeBlock( packetizer_t *p_pack, block_t **pp_bl
             block_Release( p_block );
             return NULL;
         }
+
+        /* What is left of this block once an access unit has been taken out
+         * of it comes straight back here, and the break belongs to the seam
+         * the block arrived on, not to the rest of the block: leaving the
+         * flag set resets the parser again for every following access unit,
+         * and each reset arms the outbound flag again, stamping another
+         * picture the decoder then acts on. */
+        p_block->i_flags &= ~BLOCK_FLAG_DISCONTINUITY;
     }
 
     if( p_block )
